// Routing source of truth for the AllAroHcpLogs update policies.
//
// The container-name prefixes that identify per-service log tables are declared
// exactly once here. The catch-all `containerLogs` table uses these helpers as a
// negative filter so it never double-counts a log that already belongs to a
// dedicated service table (spec R6: each log lands in exactly one table).
//
// Adding a new service table = add its prefix to KnownServiceContainerPrefixes()
// and add one sibling .kql file with a positive `container_name startswith`
// filter. Nothing in Fluent Bit changes.
//
// This file is numeric-prefixed (01_) so it is created before the target-table
// policies that reference these helpers (the validator sorts files; the Bicep
// deployment orders the foundation scripts ahead of the table scripts).
.create-or-alter function with (skipvalidation = "true", docstring = "Container-name prefixes routed to dedicated service tables")
KnownServiceContainerPrefixes() {
    datatable(prefix: string)
    [
        "aro-hcp-frontend",
        "aro-hcp-backend",
        "clusters-service",
        "fleet-controller",
        "kube-applier",
        "kube-events",
    ]
}

// Anchored alternation regex (^(a|b|c)) built from the prefix list, used by the
// catch-all so "container_name matches regex" reproduces the forwarder's old
// per-prefix "startswith" routing from a single source of truth.
.create-or-alter function with (skipvalidation = "true", docstring = "Anchored regex matching any known service container prefix")
KnownServiceContainerPrefixRegex() {
    toscalar(KnownServiceContainerPrefixes() | summarize strcat("^(", strcat_array(make_list(prefix), "|"), ")"))
}
